# REST / MCP parity

Every public REST control capability is `PARITY_REQUIRED` unless an ADR marks it `REST_ONLY_PROTOCOL` or `MCP_ONLY_PROTOCOL`.

- Same domain types, validation, authz, side effects, redaction, and error taxonomy.
- Update the capability registry, OpenAPI, MCP manifest, and parity tests in the same change.
- Do not ship REST first with MCP "later", or the reverse.
- Health/live/ready may stay REST-only. MCP prompts may stay MCP-only.
- MailDev relay is `PARITY_REQUIRED` when outgoing is configured. Do not omit it from MCP.
- mcp-integration-lab examples keep outgoing off.
